From f27c103ca7786b37f1e41a5f6194faa37de4e216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:52:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tier 1: the convention's rarer aggregate shapes (#141)

A by-value aggregate's parts now come from one function,
tier1_select_parts_of, as Tier 0's tier0_parts_of has them. A part with
no register is in its location's stack slot:

- a SPLIT location's other part, where a register clang doesn't count
  (an _Atomic scalar's or nullptr_t's) left LLVM without one for it;
- a STACK location's high or low eightbyte alone (HIGH, LOW), the other
  eightbyte being padding.

In registers, a high eightbyte of padding takes none, and with HIGH the
only register holds eightbyte 1. Results take HIGH the same way
(tier1_select_result_parts).

The entry stores a parameter's slot part into its copy through the
scratch register. A call copies an argument's slot part from its
address into the outgoing slot, and stages only its register parts.

Still refused: an ignored aggregate, and the shapes only vectors make
(a part in a vector register whole, a DEMOTED result).

test-checker-driver's fixtures of two units share one harness now, and
gain the rarer shapes' fixture: HIGH and LOW in registers and slots,
and SPLIT integer and double-long pairs, both ways round, against
clang -O0's build.

